// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-11-02 (Monday): Hindustani raga of the day — RAGA KALYAN
// ============================================================================
// Weekly rotation slot: Monday = one of the 10 parent thaats. The first full
// lap of the rotation closed on 2026-10-26 (Bilawal) after covering all 10
// thaats once (Kalyan 08-24, Bhairavi 08-31, Khamaj 09-07, Bhairav/22-shruti
// 09-14, Kafi 09-21, Todi 09-28, Marwa 10-05, Poorvi 10-12, Asavari 10-19,
// Bilawal 10-26). Today starts lap two. The last five Mondays (Todi, Marwa,
// Poorvi, Asavari, Bilawal) are avoided; Kalyan, last touched 10 weeks ago,
// is well clear of that window. This is a genuine rewrite, not a repost of
// 08-24's file — that original predates both the synth-basics correction
// (MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §2.5, it used gm_pad_warm/gm_flute) and the phrase-
// development discipline (it was one flat 12-step run, no alternating
// phrases, no retrograde) this project now holds every raga day to.
//
// THEORY NOTES:
// Kalyan's swaras: S R G M# P D N  (all shuddh except tivra/sharp Ma)
//   -> semitone offsets from tonic: 0, 2, 4, 6, 7, 9, 11 — this IS the exact
//      interval set of the Western "lydian" mode, confirmed against
//      tonaljs's own scale-type data (same discipline as every other
//      verified thaat here) — no substitution needed.
//   -> tonic kept at D, the same pitch 08-24 used for this raga specifically
//      (continuity for Kalyan itself, not a reused OTHER raga's tonic —
//      Bhairavi/E, Khamaj/G, Bhairav/A, Kafi/A, Todi/C, Marwa/F, Poorvi/B,
//      Asavari/Eb, Bilawal/Bb cover the rest of the wheel).
//   -> scale degree numbers used in n() below map like this in "D:lydian":
//        0=S(D)  1=R(E)  2=G(F#)  3=M#(G#)  4=P(A)  5=D(B)  6=N(C#)  7=S'(D5)
//   -> vadi (dominant) = Ga = degree 2, samvadi (sub-dominant) = Ni = degree 6
//      (the commonly cited pairing for Kalyan, same hedge every other thaat
//      file here uses about vadi/samvadi sourcing).
//   -> Kalyan's defining move is approaching the tivra Ma from Ga and turning
//      straight back (the "G M# G" turn), not a straight scalar climb
//      through it — the sharp 4th reads as a held, savored color tone, not
//      a passing note. That turn anchors phrase A/C below.
//
// MELODY — four alternating phrases (the device now established across
// recent raga Mondays), real leaps (mostly thirds, scale-degree jumps of 2),
// a literal retrograde, and anchoring on vadi/samvadi rather than a flat run:
//   phrase A (CALL): S ~ G M# G P ~ N  ->  n: 0 ~ 2 3 2 4 ~ 6
//     -> opens on Sa, rests, then the idiomatic G-M#-G turn around the vadi
//        (touching, not passing through, the tivra Ma), leaps a third up to
//        Pa, rests, leaps a third up again to the samvadi — ends open.
//   phrase B (RESPONSE/CLIMAX): G ~ P N S' ~ N P  ->  n: 2 ~ 4 6 7 ~ 6 4
//     -> from the vadi, climbs in thirds through Pa and the samvadi to the
//        octave peak, rests on the peak, then falls back through the
//        samvadi and a third further down to Pa — tension continues, no
//        resolution yet. (No tivra Ma in this phrase — see ARRANGEMENT.)
//   phrase C (retrograde of A — the required jazz-improv device, literal
//     reverse of A's full event list including its rests): N ~ P G M# G ~ S
//     ->  n: 6 ~ 4 2 3 2 ~ 0 — the only phrase that lands on the tonic,
//         giving the rotation its one real resolution.
//   phrase D (retrograde of B): P N ~ S' N P ~ G  ->  n: 4 6 ~ 7 6 4 ~ 2
//     -> closes each lap of the rotation back on the vadi, open again,
//        so the loop into A feels like a continuation.
//   rotation <A B C D>, 4 cycles per full statement, 16 cycles total = 4
//   full statements.
//
// ARRANGEMENT — two layers only (drone + lead), per MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §10's
// "fewer layers, each with one job" over stacking more modulation:
//   - DRONE: tonic + fifth (d2/a2), the standard tanpura tuning (Kalyan's Pa
//     is a full, unscarce member of the raga, unlike Marwa's — no retuning
//     needed). Sine, the purest waveform, per MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §2.5 — no
//     gm_sitar/gm_voice_oohs. Slow attack/release so it swells rather than
//     starting abruptly.
//   - LEAD: `supersaw` — reused from Bhairavi (08-31), but shaped toward its
//     opposite character: Bhairavi's supersaw was a fast-attack, short-decay
//     pluck standing in for sitar buzz; this one swells in with a slightly
//     longer attack/sustain, reading as a soaring sung (khayal) line rather
//     than a struck one — Kalyan's own character (bright, open, lyrical),
//     not a re-skin of Bhairavi's devotional pluck.
//   - AUTOMATION, tied directly to the raga's own color tone rather than a
//     generic sweep: resonance (`lpq`) is stepped per-phrase, `<12 4 12 4>`
//     for A/B/C/D — HIGH only on the two phrases that actually carry the
//     tivra Ma turn (A, C), low on the two that don't (B, D). The resonant
//     ring is reserved for the exact moments the sharp 4th sounds, instead
//     of an LFO sweeping independently of the melody (the weakness
//     MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md flagged on 27 Aug 2026 — "random notes on a wah").
//     Cutoff stays fixed (no second automated parameter) — one meaningful
//     piece of automation, not several stacked for their own sake.
//
// PERCUSSION CHECK (MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md's standing question, asked explicitly
// every time): this is a short alap-style exposition over a drone, the same
// shape as every raga Monday since the 09-08/09-09 lesson except Khamaj,
// which earned its keherwa theka from its own light-classical dance
// register. Kalyan is a serious evening (sandhiprakash) raga with no such
// dance-tala tradition attached — no drum layer here, decided explicitly
// rather than defaulted.
//
// This is a DAILY quick clip, not a flagship set — one continuous pattern,
// no alap/jor/jhala arc. setcpm(48) * 16 cycles = 20s (60/48 = 1.25s/cycle).
// ============================================================================

setcpm(48)
let CYCLES = 16 // 16 * 60/48 = 20s

stack(
  // drone: tonic + fifth (S and P), sine — purest waveform, tanpura
  // convention, see ARRANGEMENT above. Slow attack/release so it swells in.
  note("<d2 a2>/4")
    .sound("sine")
    .gain(.22)
    .room(4.5)
    .attack(2).release(3),

  // melody: CALL (turn around vadi + leaps) / CLIMAX (leaps to the octave) /
  // its retrograde (the one phrase that resolves to Sa) / CLIMAX's
  // retrograde (closes open, on the vadi) — see MELODY note above.
  n("<[0 ~ 2 3 2 4 ~ 6] [2 ~ 4 6 7 ~ 6 4] [6 ~ 4 2 3 2 ~ 0] [4 6 ~ 7 6 4 ~ 2]>")
    .scale("D:lydian")
    .sound("supersaw")
    .attack(.03).decay(.18).sustain(.25).release(.2)
    .cutoff(2000)
    .resonance("<12 4 12 4>") // <- rings only on the tivra-Ma turn phrases (A, C)
    .sometimes(x => x.ply(2)) // <- improv hook: occasional ornament
    .gain(.42)
    .room(2.8)
    .delay(.15)
)
